---
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Figures first',
    text: 'People open Sonar-DB to read quantities: pallets on hold, deliveries due, invoices overdue. Type stays small and steady, and hierarchy comes from weight and color, so a column of figures scans in one pass.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Measured, not picked',
    text: 'Neutrals come from one formula, text levels from contrast targets, springs from a duration and a bounce. A value that can be explained can be extended without guessing.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Calm by default, expressive on purpose',
    text: 'Motion settles without overshoot and color is reserved for meaning. The Material 3 Expressive character shows in shape and in two moments: dropping a card into place and a confirmed success.',
  },
  {
    title: 'One system at every width',
    text: 'From a 402 px phone to a five-column ultra-wide monitor, the same tokens and the same components. Layouts are derived from the desktop reading order rather than designed five times.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Accessible by contract',
    text: 'Contrast targets are written down and tested on every build. Touch targets are 48 px, status never relies on color alone, and reduced motion is respected.',
  },
]

const naming = [
  { name: '--sonar-palette-neutral-24', reads: 'palette-{family}-{tone}', note: 'Describes appearance. Never used by components.' },
  { name: '--sonar-color-text-tertiary', reads: 'color-{role}-{level}', note: 'Describes purpose. Values change with the theme.' },
  { name: '--sonar-color-on-accent-tonal', reads: 'color-on-{fill}', note: 'Content placed on a colored fill.' },
  { name: '--sonar-color-state-hover', reads: 'color-state-{interaction}', note: 'Translucent layer added on interaction.' },
  { name: '--sonar-type-title-lg', reads: 'type-{role}-{size}', note: 'A font shorthand; tracking is -tracking.' },
  { name: '--sonar-motion-spatial-fast-easing', reads: 'motion-{kind}-{speed}-{part}', note: 'Duration and easing come in pairs.' },
]

---

<Docs title="Principles and governance" description="What the Sonar-DB design system optimizes for, how its tokens are organized, named, versioned and tested.">
  <PageHeader
    title="Principles and governance"
    lead="What the system optimizes for, and the rules that keep it coherent as it grows: how tokens are organized and named, how themes work, what is tested, and how changes are versioned."
  />

  <Section title="Principles" id="principles">
    <ul class="principles" role="list">
      {
        principles.map(({ title, text }) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Three tiers" id="tiers">
    <p class="prose">
      Tokens are layered. Each tier only refers to the one below it, so a palette change reaches every component through the
      roles, and a component never hard-codes a color.
    </p>
    <figure class="tiers">
      <ol role="list">
        <li>
          <h3>Palette</h3>
          <p>Raw colors, named by hue and tone. The same in both themes.</p>
          <code>--sonar-palette-neutral-21</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Roles</h3>
          <p>What a value is for. The themes are two sets of values for the same roles.</p>
          <code>--sonar-color-text-default</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Components</h3>
          <p>Components read roles. Component-specific tokens arrive with the components.</p>
          <code>.row-label {'{'} color: var(…) {'}'}</code>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption class="visually-hidden">Palette feeds roles, roles feed components.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Naming" id="naming">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Every custom property starts with <code>--sonar-</code>, then goes from general to specific. Palette names describe
        what a color looks like; every other name describes what it is for, so a role keeps its name when its value changes.
        Names are in English, in full words, without abbreviations.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap" data-scroll-region data-label="Naming examples">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Naming examples</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Example</th><th scope="col">Pattern</th><th scope="col">Note</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            naming.map(({ name, reads, note }) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>{name}</code></th>
                <td><code>{reads}</code></td>
                <td>{note}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Themes" id="themes">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Light and dark define the same roles with different values. Without any attribute, the system follows the operating
        system. <code>data-theme="light"</code> or <code>data-theme="dark"</code> forces a theme on the element and everything
        inside it, which is how this site shows both themes side by side.
      </p>
      <p>
        The dark theme is not an inversion. Its text levels are chosen to reach the same contrast on dark surfaces as the
        light ones do on light surfaces, so a role reads with the same weight in both.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Accessibility" id="accessibility">
    <p class="prose">
      The system aims at WCAG 2.2 AA. Contrast is a contract in the tokens package, tested in both themes on every build;
      focus, target sizes, motion, keyboard and screen readers are built into every component.
      <a href="/foundations/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> sets out each commitment, the measured ratios and how they are checked.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Versioning" id="versioning">
    <ul class="prose">
      <li><strong>Patch</strong>: a value adjusted without a visible change (under 1 ΔE), or documentation.</li>
      <li><strong>Minor</strong>: new tokens, new roles, new components.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Major</strong>: a token renamed, removed or given a different meaning. The old name is kept for one minor
        release, marked <code>$deprecated</code> in the token source, before it goes.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="prose">
      What changed in each release is in the <a href="/resources/changelog/">changelog</a>; how to propose a token or a
      component, in <a href="/resources/contributing/">Contributing</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>

</Docs>

<style>
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--sonar-space-32) var(--sonar-space-40);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .principles li {
    padding-top: var(--sonar-space-16);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--sonar-color-accent);
  }

  .principles h3,
  .tiers h3 {
    font: var(--sonar-type-title-md);
    letter-spacing: var(--sonar-type-title-md-tracking);
  }

  .principles p {
    margin-top: var(--sonar-space-8);
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-secondary);
    font: var(--site-prose);
  }

  /* Stacked by default; three in a row once each can be 240 px wide */
  .tiers {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .tiers ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sonar-space-24);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .tiers li {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--sonar-space-20) var(--sonar-space-24);
    border-radius: var(--sonar-shape-corner-medium);
    background: var(--sonar-color-surface-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sonar-elevation-1);
  }

  /* The arrow between tiers (palette → roles → components) only exists in a row, where it reads as one */
  @container (width >= 784px) {
    .tiers ol {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--sonar-space-32);
    }

    .tiers li + li::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      left: calc(-1 * var(--sonar-space-32) + 8px);
      width: 16px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--sonar-color-border-emphasis);
    }
  }

  .tiers p {
    margin: var(--sonar-space-6) 0 var(--sonar-space-12);
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-secondary);
    font: var(--sonar-type-body-md);
  }

  .tiers code {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-accent);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    /* One axis only: wide content scrolls sideways; nothing scrolls or bounces up and down */
    overflow: auto hidden;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    border-radius: var(--sonar-shape-corner-medium);
    background: var(--sonar-color-surface-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sonar-elevation-1);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font: var(--sonar-type-body-md);
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: var(--sonar-space-10) var(--sonar-space-16);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sonar-color-divider);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  thead th {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-tertiary);
    font: var(--sonar-type-label-md);
    letter-spacing: var(--sonar-type-label-md-tracking);
  }

  tbody th {
    font-weight: inherit;
  }

  td {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-secondary);
  }

  table code {
    font: 500 12px/1.4 var(--sonar-font-family-mono);
  }
</style>
